prompt: Production of a product may be split among any subset of the four devices A, B, C, or D. Each activated device incurs its setup cost once and may produce up to its processing capacity. The combined production across all devices must equal 2000 units; the entire order does not have to be processed on a single device. Production quantities are modeled as nonnegative continuous variables. The setup completion cost for each device when it is activated, the unit cost of production for the product, and the maximum processing capacity for each device are known as shown in 6.csv. How can the total cost be minimized to produce 2000 units of the product? Try to establish a mathematical model.
Type: Mixture

